      "Technically, we usually recommend separate country versions: /nz/ and /au/ folders on one domain, or a .co.nz site paired with a .com.au site. Each version has its own currency, tax settings, shipping rules and spelling where it differs, and hreflang tags tell Google which one belongs to which country. Shopify Markets and similar features can handle part of this for stores; custom sites handle it in the build. Afterpay works in both countries, which keeps checkout familiar on both sides. If you are selling into Australia, our <a href=\"/australia/\">Australia page</a> covers that market in more depth.",
